# OpenEVV sound map: Finnish (eSpeak NG voice urj/fi), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides r l j w
schwa @
secondary 2

# the melody: peak; a question that wants yes or no: fall
accent f0=own range=72 shape=0 accent=21 accent2=10 unstressed=-6 decl=8 declmax=30 fs=-18 fw=-12 fc=10 fe=-12 fq=-8 qreg=14 span=2 stressed=94 weak=106 stop=1

# the words a question is asked with, which is not the question that wants yes or no
whwords first kuka mikä mitä missä milloin miten miksi kuinka
whwords first kumpi kenen mistä mihin ketä

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

